usage: mplpb-combined [-h] [--version]
                      {ask,gate,validate,list,show,history,write,revise,derive,ratify,withdraw,seal,index,killtest,candidates,tag-procedure}
                      ...

A closed local ledger of pages. Return, ambiguous, or not in corpus. Never
blend.

positional arguments:
  {ask,gate,validate,list,show,history,write,revise,derive,ratify,withdraw,seal,index,killtest,candidates,tag-procedure}
    ask                 answer one question from the folder, or refuse
    gate                gather separate source pages with provenance; never
                        synthesize
    validate            check every page against the format; exit 1 on error
    list                list records
    show                read one record by id, retired or not
    history             walk a supersession chain
    write               write a new page
    revise              write a new page and retire the old one
    derive              write a page derived from others; depth goes up by one
    ratify              a named person signs a page; depth returns to 0
    withdraw            retire a page with no successor
    seal                adopt hand-written or earlier-format pages: add hashes
    index               rebuild index.html for people
    killtest            strip the declared fields and compare
    candidates          inspect legacy lexical candidates; not supported
                        answers
    tag-procedure       draft numbered-step tags without promoting them to
                        evidence

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
